Package: profilemlm
Title: Multilevel Profile Analysis of Person Judgment Data
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Johannes", "Zimmermann", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "johannes.zimmermann@uni-kassel.de",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6975-2356")),
    person("Nele M.", "Wessels", role = "dtc",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0259-0713", "data sets wessels_judgments and wessels_items")))
Description: Prepares, fits, compares and visualises multilevel profile analyses of
    person judgment data: cross-classified linear mixed-effects models in the tradition
    of the Social Accuracy Model (Biesanz, 2010) in which judgment profiles are
    regressed on the normative and distinctive components of a criterion profile,
    with random effects for perceivers, targets, dyads and items, and with item,
    perceiver, target and dyadic predictors of profile agreement. Further predictor
    profiles (e.g., the perceivers' self-ratings, for assumed similarity) and designs
    with unconnected pairs are supported. Includes data
    preparation from survey exports and tidy input objects, design detection,
    identifiability-aware formula construction, random-effects diagnostics,
    marginal-effect plots, standardized effect sizes, a simulation function and the
    data of Wessels et al.
    (2020, 2025), Study 2. Models are estimated by maximum likelihood with lme4 or,
    with the same formulas and the same output tables, by Bayesian sampling with brms.
